      "problem": "What is the volume of a sphere whose diameter is $8\\,\\text{mm}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{8}{2}=4\\,\\text{mm}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\cdot {4}^{3}=\\frac{256}{3}\\pi \\,{\\text{mm}}^{3}.\n$$",
